{
  "id": "zstd-backend-selection-in-net-encoding-py-and-pyproject-depe",
  "title": "zstd backend selection in net/encoding.py and pyproject dependency",
  "kind": "location",
  "answers": [
    "Where is zstd compression implemented?",
    "How to switch zstd library to stdlib compression.zstd?",
    "Where is zstandard dependency declared?"
  ],
  "body": "- zstd is used only in `mitmproxy/net/encoding.py`: top-level import `zstandard as zstd`, plus `decode_zstd` (ZstdDecompressor().stream_reader(BytesIO, read_across_frames=True).read(); empty input returns b\"\") and `encode_zstd` (ZstdCompressor(level=1).compress).\n- Dependency pin lives in `pyproject.toml` (`zstandard>=0.25,<=0.25.0`); uv.lock would need regeneration if the marker changes.\n- Existing test `test/mitmproxy/net/test_encoding.py:test_zstd` round-trips encode/decode (incl. multi-frame), so covers whichever backend loads.\n- API differences: stdlib `compression.zstd` has module-level `compress(data, level=)` and `decompress(data)` (handles concatenated frames); zstandard uses ctx objects.",
  "tags": [
    "zstd",
    "encoding",
    "dependency"
  ],
